  "comment": "SEVENTEENTH PACK. Swahili: NOUN CLASSES, and the agreement runs the OTHER WAY. `count_agreement` asks which form a NOUN takes at a count; Swahili's noun never changes — the NUMERAL and the ADJECTIVE change their PREFIX by the noun's class (kitabu kimoja / mtu mmoja / vitabu viwili). There is no field for a noun's class, none for a dependent word's agreement, and `verb_rule` can only say stem+ending while every Swahili affix is a PREFIX. The phenomenon is SHOWN as whole phrases and is judged by nothing. Multi-word numerals (kumi na moja) are unreadable to the arithmetic judge, as Turkish's «on bir» already was. TIER 1.",
